# What NOT to put in the .vsix.
#
# `node_modules/` is deliberately absent from this list. `vscode-languageclient`
# is a runtime dependency — the extension calls it on every activation — and
# `vsce` already prunes devDependencies for us. Excluding node_modules here
# produces a .vsix that packages cleanly, installs cleanly, and then throws
# "Cannot find module 'vscode-languageclient/node'" the first time a .zen file
# is opened. It was written that way once; this comment is why it is not.
.vscode/**
src/**
out/**/*.map
tsconfig.json
.gitignore
**/*.ts
!out/**/*.js
